9baee","quote":"Revenues were US$82.6 million in the second quarter of 2026, compared with US$84.6 million in the second quarter of 2025, primarily due to a decrease in paying users attributable to the impact of recent geopolitical events in the broader region, partially offset by an increase in revenues from games services.","context":"Revenues","section":"","block":31,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-354652","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-18","reportDate":"2026-08-18","cik":"0001794350","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1794350/000119312526354652/yala-ex99_1.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/01451915893f7f2c81a0e9dcb4140c2006a3afb86f77c1b5a11b28f59a64b901.bin","sha256":"01451915893f7f2c81a0e9dcb4140c2006a3afb86f77c1b5a11b28f59a64b901"}},{"id":"a21213ed546331b69b6923545a0b22db2451715530b5d43838f8fd517cc97bf7","quote":"Cost of revenues was US$26.8 million in the second quarter of 2026, a 4.1% decrease from US$27.9 million in the second quarter of 2025, primarily due to lower commission fees paid to third-party payment platforms. Cost of revenues as a percentage of total revenues decreased to 32.4% in the second quarter of 2026 from 33.0% in the second quarter of 2025.","context":"Total costs and expenses were US$63.2 million in the second quarter of 2026, compared with US$53.9 million in the second quarter of 2025.","section":"","block":35,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-354652","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-18","reportDate":"2026-08-18","cik":"0001794350","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1794350/000119312526354652/yala-ex99_1.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/01451915893f7f2c81a0e9dcb4140c2006a3afb86f77c1b5a11b28f59a64b901.bin","sha256":"01451915893f7f2c81a0e9dcb4140c2006a3afb86f77c1b5a11b28f59a64b901"}},{"id":"31994bb1a1766f34e9a2ca5cbe4ec8ea8772ad0edf6b78979e769901d64e0e1c","quote":"Selling and marketing expenses were US$17.8 million in the second quarter of 2026, a 106.0% increase from US$8.7 million in the second quarter of 2025, primarily due to higher advertising and market promotion expenses attributable to the Company’s continued user acquisition efforts and support for new games. Selling and marketing expenses as a percentage of total revenues increased to 21.6% in the second quarter of 2026 from 10.2% in the second quarter of 2025.","context":"Cost of revenues was US$26.8 million in the second quarter of 2026, a 4.1% decrease from US$27.9 million in the second quarter of 2025, primarily due to lower commission fees paid to third-party payment platforms. Cost of revenues as a percentage of total revenues decreased to 32.4% in the second quarter of 2026 from 33.0% in the second quarter of 2025.","section":"","block":36,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-354652","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-18","reportDate":"2026-08-18","cik":"0001794350","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1794350/000119312526354652/yala-ex99_1.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/01451915893f7f2c81a0e9dcb4140c2006a3afb86f77c1b5a11b28f59a64b901.bin","sha256":"01451915893f7f2c81a0e9dcb4140c2006a3afb86f77c1b5a11b28f59a64b901"}},{"id":"083f147c62a1428b36ade574c09511d71c8772919c5118d631b7298832dbf406","quote":"General and administrative expenses were US$8.6 million in the second quarter of 2026, a 4.0% decrease from US$9.0 million in the second quarter of 2025, primarily due to a decrease in incentive compensation, partially offset by an increase in foreign exchange loss. General and administrative expenses as a percentage of total revenues slightly decreased to 10.5% in the second quarter of 2026 from 10.6% in the second quarter of 2025.","context":"Selling and marketing expenses were US$17.8 million in the second quarter of 2026, a 106.0% increase from US$8.7 million in the second quarter of 2025, primarily due to higher advertising and market promotion expenses attributable to the Company’s continued user acquisition efforts and support for new games. Selling and marketing expenses as a percentage of total revenues increased to 21.6% in the second quarter of 2026 from 10.2% in the second quarter of 2025.","section":"","block":37,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-354652","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-18","reportDate":"2026-08-18","cik":"0001794350","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1794350/000119312526354652/yala-ex99_1.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/01451915893f7f2c81a0e9dcb4140c2006a3afb86f77c1b5a11b28f59a64b901.bin","sha256":"01451915893f7f2c81a0e9dcb4140c2006a3afb86f77c1b5a11b28f59a64b901"}},{"id":"63cd676d77348a174d680f85d077acf6aa5b9682cb2932fd4a4443d3b621153d","quote":"Technology and product development expenses were US$9.9 million in the second quarter of 2026, an 18.9% increase from US$8.3 million in the second quarter of 2025, primarily due to an increase in salaries and benefits for our technology and product development staff, driven by an increase in headcount to support the development of new businesses and our product portfolio expansion. Technology and product development expenses as a percentage of total revenues increased to 12.0% in the second quarter of 2026 from 9.9% in the second quarter of 2025.","context":"General and administrative expenses were US$8.6 million in the second quarter of 2026, a 4.0% decrease from US$9.0 million in the second quarter of 2025, primarily due to a decrease in incentive compensation, partially offset by an increase in foreign exchange loss. General and administrative expenses as a percentage of total revenues slightly decreased to 10.5% in the second quarter of 2026 from 10.6% in the second quarter of 2025.","section":"","block":38,"t